---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Lumey Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Lumey reading companion and book tracking app."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Lumey Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: June 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey is a reading companion application designed to help users track
          books, manage reading goals, organize personal libraries, monitor
          reading progress, and build a more enjoyable reading experience.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains what information Lumey stores, how it is
          used, and how you remain in control of your information.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data You Create</h2>
        <p>
          Information created within Lumey may include books, authors, reading
          progress, ratings, reviews, notes, reading goals, reading sessions,
          reading history, tags, collections, achievements, points, and user
          preferences.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information is stored locally on your device and may synchronize
          through your personal iCloud account if CloudKit synchronization is
          enabled.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>iCloud & CloudKit</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may use Apple's CloudKit framework to synchronize information
          between your Apple devices through your personal iCloud account.
        </p>

        <p>
          The developer of Lumey does not have access to your private CloudKit
          database.
        </p>

        <p>
          Apple's handling of iCloud data is governed by Apple's privacy policy.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Library Management</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may store information related to books in your personal library,
          including titles, authors, reading status, formats, page counts,
          genres, ratings, and other information you choose to record.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information is used solely to provide library organization and
          reading management features.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Reading Progress</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may store reading progress, pages completed, reading sessions,
          completion dates, reading history, and related statistics.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information is used exclusively to provide reading progress
          tracking, statistics, goals, and insights within the app.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Reading Goals</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may allow users to create reading goals related to books, pages,
          minutes, authors, genres, series, or other reading objectives.
        </p>

        <p>
          Goal information is stored solely to provide goal tracking and
          progress reporting features.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Ratings, Reviews & Notes</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may store ratings, reviews, reading notes, reflections, quotes,
          and other information entered by the user.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information remains private unless explicitly shared by the user.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Reading Statistics</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may generate reading statistics, reading streaks, completion
          reports, reading trends, progress charts, and other insights based on
          information you choose to record.
        </p>

        <p>
          These calculations exist solely to provide personal reading insights
          and motivation.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Book Information</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may allow users to manually enter book information or retrieve
          publicly available book metadata from approved third-party sources.
        </p>

        <p>
          Retrieved information may include book titles, authors, descriptions,
          publication information, genres, cover images, and ISBN data.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Achievements & Rewards</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may include optional points, achievements, streaks, milestones,
          and reward systems designed to encourage reading consistency and
          engagement.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information remains private to your account and is not used for
          advertising, profiling, or marketing purposes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Notifications</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may use local notifications to provide reminders related to
          reading goals, reading sessions, streaks, challenges, and other
          reading activities.
        </p>

        <p>Notification scheduling occurs directly on your device.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Widgets</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may provide Home Screen and Lock Screen widgets displaying
          reading progress, books currently being read, reading goals, streaks,
          achievements, and reading statistics.
        </p>

        <p>
          Widget information is shared locally between the app and widget
          extensions using Apple's App Group system.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Analytics & Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey does not sell personal information and does not use third-party
          advertising networks or behavioral advertising systems.
        </p>

        <p>
          Reading history, ratings, notes, and reading activity information are
          not shared with advertisers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>In-App Purchases</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey may offer optional premium features or subscriptions through
          Apple's StoreKit framework.
        </p>

        <p>
          Payment processing is handled entirely by Apple. Lumey does not
          collect, store, or have access to payment information, billing
          information, or credit card numbers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Lumey is not directed toward children under the age of 13 and does not
          knowingly collect personal information from children.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          You maintain control over your information at all times. Books,
          reading history, goals, ratings, reviews, notes, statistics, and other
          content may be deleted directly within the app.
        </p>

        <p>
          Deleting the app removes locally stored data from your device. If
          CloudKit synchronization is enabled, synced information may also be
          managed through your Apple ID and iCloud settings.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This privacy policy may occasionally be updated to reflect new
          features, legal requirements, platform changes, or improvements to the
          app. Updated versions will be published on this page with a revised
          effective date.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy or how Lumey handles
          your information, you can contact:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--overlay-gradient-accent);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
